<spell-notebook "grid theming">
	<header level="1">
		Grid
		<header>A grid is used to harmonize negative space in a layout.</>
	</>
	<grid-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-grid-*` tokens: set one on the grid element, on any ancestor (a region, `:root`), or
			on the grid's box through `::part(grid)` (or on `.ui.grid` in your app stylesheet); its rows and columns follow.
			They inherit into the shadow roots, where the sheet reads each through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks
			them.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every grid on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-grid-divider-color: var(--ui-border-color-strong);
			}
			/* one grid */
			ui-grid.roomy {
			  --ui-grid-gutter: 3em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`spacing="lg"` and `spacing="compact"` swap in their own gutter tokens (`--ui-grid-relaxed-gutter`, `--ui-grid-compact-gutter`
				...), whatever the base gutter; `celled` reads the `--ui-grid-celled-*` ones. Never set the `--_ui-*` /
				`--_grid-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-grid" playground>
				<ui-grid>
					<ui-column width="4">
						<ui-text paragraph>Four wide</>
					</>
					<ui-column width="4">
						<ui-text paragraph>Four wide</>
					</>
					<ui-column width="4">
						<ui-text paragraph>Four wide</>
					</>
					<ui-column width="4">
						<ui-text paragraph>Four wide</>
					</>
					<ui-column width="8">
						<ui-text paragraph>Eight wide</>
					</>
					<ui-column width="8">
						<ui-text paragraph>Eight wide</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
